            ok = true;
            // The single assertion must read c; we assert that the returned boolean equals
            // whether the public getter owner() matches newOwner. This is the universal rule:
            // on the reference, whenever the call returns it reports success (true) iff owner==newOwner.
            // We observe this by checking c.owner() == newOwner implies ret == true, and vice versa.
            // Combine into a single boolean equality and assertTrue on it.
            assertTrue((c.owner() == newOwner) == ret);
